---
// 2026 federal-tax-credit correction notice.
// The 30% federal residential ITC (Section 25D) expired Dec 31, 2025 (OBBBA)
// for owned systems. Content written before that bakes the credit into cost
// and savings figures. Render this above any cost/incentive content written
// during the ITC era so the page never states an outdated incentive unflagged.
---
<div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-5 my-8">
  <p class="font-display font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-2">⚠️ 2026 update on the federal tax credit</p>
  <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-0">
    The <strong>30% federal residential solar tax credit (Section 25D) expired on December 31, 2025</strong> for systems you buy with cash or a loan. Cost and savings figures on this page that assume that credit may be out of date. Two things still apply: <strong>Nevada's sales-tax and property-tax exemptions</strong> and <strong>NV Energy net metering</strong>, and systems on a <strong>lease or PPA may still qualify for a federal incentive through the end of 2027</strong>. For numbers that reflect today's incentives, <a href="/#get-quote" class="text-brand-orange font-semibold">book a free review</a> and talk to a tax professional about your situation.
  </p>
</div>
